<title>GEORGIA: SOCCER-GEORGIA NAMES SQUAD FOR POLAND GAME.</title>
<headline>SOCCER-GEORGIA NAMES SQUAD FOR POLAND GAME.</headline>
<dateline>TBILISI 1997-06-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Georgia on Wednesday named the</p>
<p>following squad for their World Cup European group two qualifier</p>
<p>in Poland on June 14:</p>
<p>Squad:</p>
<p>Goalkeepers - Irakli Zoidze, (Dynamo Tbilisi), Nika</p>
<p>Togonidze (Dynamo Batumi)</p>
<p>Defenders - Kakha Tskhadadze, Levan Kobiashvili (both Alania</p>
<p>Vladikavkaz, Russia), Nugzar Lobdzhanidze (CSKA Moscow, Russia),</p>
<p>Georgy Chikhradze (Shakhtar Donetsk, Ukraine), Kakha Kaladze</p>
<p>(Dynamo Tbilisi), Gela Shekiladze (Dynamo Batumi)</p>
<p>Midfielders - Kakha Gogichaishvili, Georgy Kiknadze, Georgy</p>
<p>Anchabadze, (all Dynamo Tbilisi), Georgy Nemsadze, Gocha</p>
<p>Dzhamarauli (both Trabzonspor, Turkey), Gocha Gakhokidze (Alania</p>
<p>Vladikavkaz), Temur Ketsbaia (Newcastle United, England), Georgy</p>
<p>Kinkladze (Manchester City, England), Temur Tugushi (Dynamo</p>
<p>Batumi)</p>
<p>Forwards - Mikhail Kavelashvili (Manchester City, England),</p>
<p>Archil Arveladze (Trabzonspor), Zaza Dzhanashia (Lokomotiv</p>
<p>Moscow, Russia).</p>
</text>
